{"id":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:thm-harmonic-mean-value","title":"hanlin:thm-harmonic-mean-value","path":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions.md","line":47,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions.tex#hanlin:thm-harmonic-mean-value","uses":["[[references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:def-mean-value-properties]]","[[references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:def-harmonic]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions.tex","label":"hanlin:thm-harmonic-mean-value","line":74,"source":"\\begin{theorem}\\label{hanlin:thm-harmonic-mean-value}\\dcref{Theorem 1.6}\\group{harmonic-functions}\n\\source{han-lin-lecture-notes:page-0008}\n\\uses{hanlin:def-mean-value-properties, hanlin:def-harmonic}\n\n\nEvery harmonic $u\\in C^2(\\Omega)$ satisfies the mean value properties.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch Apply the divergence theorem on $B_\\rho(x)$ to obtain\n\\[\n\\int_{B_\\rho(x)}\\Delta u=\\rho^{n-1}\\frac d{d\\rho}\n\\int_{|\\omega|=1}u(x+\\rho\\omega)\\,d\\sigma_\\omega.\n\\]\nThe left side vanishes, so the spherical integral is independent of $\\rho$.\nIts limit at $\\rho=0$ is $\\omega_nu(x)$, giving the spherical identity; the\nball identity follows from Remark~\\ref{hanlin:remark-mean-value-equivalent}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-68616e6c696e3a74686d2d6861726d6f6e69632d6d65616e2d76616c7565\"></span><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. Theorem 1.6</span></span>\\group harmonic-functions <span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">han-lin-lecture-notes:page-0008</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FHanLinLectureNotes%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch01-harmonic-functions%23hanlin%3Adef-mean-value-properties\">↗ hanlin:def-mean-value-properties</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FHanLinLectureNotes%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch01-harmonic-functions%23hanlin%3Adef-harmonic\">↗ hanlin:def-harmonic</a> <p></p>Every harmonic <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u\\in C^2(\\Omega )$\">$u\\in C^2(\\Omega )$</span> satisfies the mean value properties.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Apply the divergence theorem on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_\\rho (x)$\">$B_\\rho (x)$</span> to obtain </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\int _{B_\\rho (x)}\\Delta u=\\rho ^{n-1}\\frac d{d\\rho } \\int _{|\\omega |=1}u(x+\\rho \\omega )\\, d\\sigma _\\omega .  \\]\">\\[  \\int _{B_\\rho (x)}\\Delta u=\\rho ^{n-1}\\frac d{d\\rho } \\int _{|\\omega |=1}u(x+\\rho \\omega )\\, d\\sigma _\\omega .  \\]</span></p><p> The left side vanishes, so the spherical integral is independent of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\rho $\">$\\rho $</span>. Its limit at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\rho =0$\">$\\rho =0$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\omega _nu(x)$\">$\\omega _nu(x)$</span>, giving the spherical identity; the ball identity follows from Remark <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FHanLinLectureNotes%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch01-harmonic-functions%23hanlin%3Aremark-mean-value-equivalent\" data-tex-node=\"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:remark-mean-value-equivalent\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-68616e6c696e3a72656d61726b2d6d65616e2d76616c75652d6571756976616c656e74\">1</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: group、sketch"]},"previous":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:def-harmonic","next":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:remark-mvp-not-smooth","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:def-mean-value-properties","title":"hanlin:def-mean-value-properties","label":"hanlin:def-mean-value-properties"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:def-harmonic","title":"hanlin:def-harmonic","label":"hanlin:def-harmonic"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:remark-mvp-not-smooth","title":"hanlin:remark-mvp-not-smooth","label":"hanlin:remark-mvp-not-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:thm-mean-value-harmonic","title":"hanlin:thm-mean-value-harmonic","label":"hanlin:thm-mean-value-harmonic"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:remark-mvp-harmonic-smooth","title":"hanlin:remark-mvp-harmonic-smooth","label":"hanlin:remark-mvp-harmonic-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:lemma-interior-gradient-1","title":"hanlin:lemma-interior-gradient-1","label":"hanlin:lemma-interior-gradient-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/HanLinLectureNotes/blueprint/src/chapters/ch01-harmonic-functions#hanlin:lemma-interior-gradient-2","title":"hanlin:lemma-interior-gradient-2","label":